          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What code would that be recorded under?",
          "answer": "The ICD-10 code for type 2 diabetes mellitus is **E11**. This code falls under Chapter 4 of the ICD-10, which covers endocrine, nutritional, and metabolic diseases. It specifically categorizes diabetes by cause, and type 2 diabetes has its own distinct code. \n\nIf a medical record indicates \"diabetes mellitus\" without specifying the type, it defaults to type 2 diabetes in coding. \n\nFor further details, you might explore the reference on coding type 2 diabetes, where it discusses the complications and subcategories related to this code. \n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
